2026-11-07T07:08:12.9052910Z [34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
2026-11-07T07:08:12.9114770Z [0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
2026-11-07T07:08:12.9116350Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
2026-11-07T07:08:12.9117240Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
2026-11-07T07:08:12.9117700Z 
2026-11-07T07:08:12.9118440Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
2026-11-07T07:08:12.9119060Z 
2026-11-07T07:08:12.9119490Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
2026-11-07T07:08:12.9120390Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
2026-11-07T07:08:12.9120860Z 
2026-11-07T07:08:12.9121160Z If you would like to
2026-11-07T07:08:12.9121890Z see the output, try like this:
2026-11-07T07:08:12.9122250Z 
2026-11-07T07:08:12.9122690Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
2026-11-07T07:08:12.9123480Z   $ sh ./install-nix
